{
  "name": "Attack gate — identity and admin",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Identity and admin API\n\nThis sits in front of the API that would change a payout destination, grant a role, or reset MFA. The webhook is that hold point. Nothing is mutated on this canvas. The last node is what that API would do.\n\n**Build state** keeps the caller's words apart from facts the directory already knows, such as MFA age, country, and scanner hits. **Attack gate** uses the attack-triage policy. A confident hostile intent is blocked. High risk or a human-review signal is held. Only a confident low-risk legitimate event is allowed. Anything else is held.\n\n**Walk the examples** runs three pinned events. Pick it from the trigger menu.\n\n1. Payout destination change after a recent MFA reset from a new country. Refused.\n2. Role grant from a new country. Refused.\n3. Add a teammate to the billing readers group. Applied.\n\nPOST /webhook/attack-identity with `text`, `request`, `actor`, `action`, `subject`, and `facts`. The stand-in matches a phrase in `text`. A real server reads the whole state, including `facts`. If Attack gate errors, this workflow stops, so Apply the change does not run.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "How to read this",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Walk the examples",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "attack-identity",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        200,
        760
      ],
      "webhookId": "attack-identity"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Separate the untrusted request from facts the caller already verified.\n// The Attack gate reads state. It does not read the webhook envelope.\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nconst event = item.body && typeof item.body === 'object' && !Array.isArray(item.body) ? item.body : item;\nconst facts = event.facts && typeof event.facts === 'object' && !Array.isArray(event.facts) ? event.facts : {};\nconst request = typeof event.request === 'string' ? event.request : '';\nconst text = typeof event.text === 'string' && event.text !== '' ? event.text : request;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    state: {\n      text,\n      request,\n      facts,\n      actor: event.actor ?? null,\n      action: event.action ?? null,\n      subject: event.subject ?? null,\n    },\n  },\n};\n"
      },
      "id": "a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Build state",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "state": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.state) }}",
        "questionSet": "custom",
        "questions": {
          "intent": {
            "type": "choice",
            "instructions": "What this event is, based on the facts in the state",
            "criteria": {
              "legitimate_ops": "Expected work by someone who should be doing it",
              "benign": "Ordinary request with no security impact",
              "account_takeover": "Signs that someone else is using an account, session, or recovery flow",
              "social_engineering": "A request to bypass, reset, or redirect a control or a payment",
              "supply_chain": "A change to build, dependency, CI, or release controls",
              "reconnaissance": "Probing for access, secrets, or weaknesses"
            }
          },
          "risk": {
            "type": "score",
            "instructions": "How much an automated action could change security, access, or data",
            "criteria": [
              "No security impact and easy to reverse",
              "Limited to one user or one record",
              "Touches authentication, secrets, or a shared control",
              "Bypasses a control, exposes data, or is hard to reverse"
            ]
          },
          "needs_human": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "A person should decide before any automated action"
          }
        },
        "rules": {
          "version": 1,
          "owner": "decision-matrix",
          "ticket": "attack-triage",
          "default_action": {
            "type": "escalate",
            "target": "human",
            "reason": "No matching rule",
            "gate": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "high_confidence": 0.85,
            "high_risk": 2
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "hold-hostile",
              "description": "A confident hostile intent is blocked before any other route",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "account_takeover",
                      "social_engineering",
                      "supply_chain",
                      "reconnaissance"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "block",
                "target": "security",
                "reason": "Hold {{answers.intent.choice}} before any automated action",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hold-uncertain",
              "description": "High risk or a human-review signal goes to a person",
              "when": {
                "any": [
                  {
                    "question": "needs_human",
                    "gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "gte": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "escalate",
                "target": "human",
                "reason": "Risk or human-review signal crossed the threshold",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "allow-legitimate",
              "description": "Only a confident, low-risk, legitimate event can be automated",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "legitimate_ops",
                      "benign"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "lt": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "allow",
                "target": "automation",
                "reason": "Allow {{answers.intent.choice}} below risk {{thresholds.high_risk}}",
                "gate": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "includeFullAnswers": true,
          "failOnNoMatch": false
        }
      },
      "id": "a1010000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Attack gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-decision-matrix.decisionMatrix",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        780,
        640
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "decisionServerApi": {
          "name": "Decision Server API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
